sentences.t:
διογενὲς Λαερτιάδη, πολυμήχαν’ Ὀδυσσεῦ,
οὕτω δὴ οἶκόνδε φίλην ἐς πατρίδα γαῖαν
αὐτίκα νῦν ἐθέλεις ἰέναι;

sentences.tr:
diogenes Laertiadē, polymēchan’ Odysseu,
houtō dē oikonde philēn es patrida gaian
autika nyn etheleis ienai;

sentences.l:
I know myself too,
full well, that than you circumspect Penelope
in looks is slighter, and in stature, to look upon face to face;

But when indeed she had shown him where tall trees had grown,
she went back to the house, Calypso, heavenly-one of goddesses,
and he set to cutting timbers;

And in it for him the goddess put a skin of dark wine,
the one, and the other, of water, a big one, and in it too provisions
in a leather sack;

Seven and ten days he sailed, crossing the open sea,
and on the eighteenth appeared the shadowy mountains
of the land of the Phaeacians, where it was nearest to him;
